Subject: [PATCH] Reuse owned unmapped intervals within the current guest image

Keep successful runtime munmap intervals in the authoritative mapping registry.
Coalesce adjacent ranges and reuse aligned first-fit intervals before memory.grow,
without inferring ownership from holes in guest heap memory. Publish reclamation
and allocation only after the host remap succeeds under the existing lock order.

Fork copies reusable ownership. Exec removes the old image intervals before
instantiation, and its existing rollback guard restores both active mappings and
reusable intervals on admission failure. Never reuse old-image heap addresses in
a fresh image. Reused mappings install the new backing and futex identity.

This is a correctness change after the source-equivalent split in 0001-0008.
The runtime patch digest and receipts change; rebuild selected carriers. The
ownership fix is generally applicable to WASIX persistent shared-file remaps.

